C03: music named without a provider plays from YouTube in the local player (MUSIC1559)

Five open Música rows name music without saying where («pon música de daft punk», «pon una cancion de michael jackson» twice, «Pon bad de michael jackson», «poneme algo de música tranqui»); the reader sent them to media.play.query, whose only provider is Spotify and whose session does not exist on this PC (owner's decision: skip). With the local YouTube playback demonstrated in MUSIC1557, the resolver sends provider-less named music to media.play.youtube («en Spotify» keeps Spotify) and the argument builder takes the named music in the person's words as the query, dropping a leading «algo de». Registry-wide recogniser diff with the real Start catalog: exactly those five rows change (media.play.query → media.play.youtube).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


